1
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:08,960
Excuse me. Can you help me?

2
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:10,770
Sure, what do you want?

3
00:00:10,770 --> 00:00:13,250
Where is 83 Wooster Street?

4
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:16,620
That's easy. Walk to the corner.

5
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:18,580
Then make a left turn.

6
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:21,600
Then walk two blocks to the traffic light.

7
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,220
Make another left to Wooster.

8
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:24,940
Thank you.

9
00:00:24,940 --> 00:00:26,870
To the corner and then a left?

10
00:00:26,870 --> 00:00:28,230
Yeah. A left.

11
00:00:28,230 --> 00:00:30,050
Hot dog? Only seventy-five cents.

12
00:00:30,050 --> 00:00:44,650
No. Thank you. I have a dinner date.

13
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:59,250
555-9470...and it's busy....

14
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:10,200
Try again.

15
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:21,160
555-9470...and it's still busy.

16
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,350
Excuse me, ma'am.

17
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:25,850
I'm looking for 83 Wooster Street.

18
00:01:25,850 --> 00:01:28,870
Yes. Wooster Street is two blocks,

19
00:01:28,870 --> 00:01:35,350
and 83 is to the right, about two houses.

20
00:01:35,350 --> 00:01:37,030
Thank you, thank you!

21
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:48,000
You're welcome.

22
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,580
Who is it?

23
00:01:49,580 --> 00:01:51,360
Harry Bennett. Is this Susan?

24
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:52,890
Yes, it is. Come up.

25
00:01:52,890 --> 00:01:55,510
I'm on the top floor.

26
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:58,530
Hello, Harry. It's nice to meet you.

27
00:01:58,530 --> 00:02:00,780
Nice to meet you, Susan.

28
00:02:00,780 --> 00:02:02,680
Sorry I'm late.

29
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:08,600
The traffic. The parking. I was lost.

30
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:10,510
What pretty flowers! Thank you.

31
00:02:10,510 --> 00:02:13,180
Oh, please come in.

32
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:16,530
Don't worry about being late. It's fine.

33
00:02:16,530 --> 00:02:20,090
Excuse the mess. I just moved here.

34
00:02:20,090 --> 00:02:23,140
Oh, I'd like you to meet my sister-in-law Marilyn.

35
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:25,580
Marilyn Stewart, this is Harry Bennett.

36
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:26,420
Pleased to meet you.

37
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:28,330
Nice to meet you, Harry.

38
00:02:28,330 --> 00:02:30,260
Are we too late for our dinner reservation?

39
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:32,470
No, the restaurant will hold our table.

40
00:02:32,470 --> 00:02:33,540
I know the owner very well.

41
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:34,640
I eat there a lot.

42
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:36,420
Do you know the phone number of the restaurant?

43
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:38,300
I'd like to call home

44
00:02:38,300 --> 00:02:39,600
and leave the number with the baby-sitter.

45
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:50,300
Sure. The number is... five five five...seventeen twenty.

46
00:02:50,300 --> 00:03:01,740
May I use the phone?

47
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:07,210
Five five five...one seven two oh. Hello?

48
00:03:07,210 --> 00:03:08,440
Hi, Michelle. It's Daddy.

49
00:03:08,440 --> 00:03:10,890
Can I speak to Betty?

50
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:15,010
I want to leave the phone number of the restaurant...

51
00:03:15,010 --> 00:03:19,980
Hi, Betty. I'll be at five five five...seventeen twenty.

52
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:24,790
OK. Thanks. See you later.

53
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:27,300
Well, that's done. Shall we go?

54
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:29,520
I'm ready. See you later, Marilyn.

55
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:31,280
Have a nice evening.

56
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,970
Bye, Marilyn. Hope to see you again.

57
00:03:32,970 --> 00:03:35,250
Me, too. Have fun!

58
00:03:35,250 --> 00:03:39,680
Thanks.

59
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:42,680
After you.
